SUMMARY:Lafayette Farmers & Artisans Market
LOCATION:Moncus Park\, 2913 Johnston Street\, Lafayette
DESCRIPTION:Lafayette Farmers & Artisans Market Every Saturday | 8:00 AM to
  12:00 PM | Moncus Park | Rain or Shine There is no better way to start a 
 Saturday in Acadiana. Every week\, the Lafayette Farmers and Artisans Mark
 et transforms the heart of Moncus Park into a lively gathering place\, whe
 re local farmers\, artisans\, and craftspeople come together to share the 
 best of our region. Wander the rows and you will find tables overflowing w
 ith just-picked produce\, local honey\, fresh flowers\, baked goods\, hand
 made crafts\, and one-of-a-kind finds from the makers who pour their heart
 s into them. Whether you come for the produce\, the people\, or simply the
  joy of a morning outdoors\, the market is where Lafayette starts its week
 end. Come hungry\, shop local\, and make a morning of it! Parking & Gettin
 g There We guide thousands of visitors in and out every Saturday morning\,
  so parking may take a few extra minutes during peak times\, but our team 
 keeps things moving all morning! Our parking lot is $2 per hour\, or free 
 for Moncus Park members. All proceeds support Moncus Park\, a nonprofit pa
 rk conservancy. Please only park at Moncus Park\, towing is strictly enfor
 ced by a third party in neighboring lots. Prefer to skip the parking altog
 ether? Walking or biking in is always a breeze! Weekly Vendor Lineup Curio
 us who's setting up shop this Saturday? Check the Lafayette Farmers & Arti
 sans Market Facebook page the Friday before market day for the full vendor
  list. Become a Vendor Interested in joining us as a farmer\, artisan\, or
  maker? The Lafayette Farmers & Artisans Market is a producer-only market\
 , meaning all products sold must be grown\, raised\, baked\, crafted\, or 
 otherwise produced by the vendor. Reselling products made by someone else 
 is not permitted. Vendor applications are accepted twice each year during 
 the following application periods: January 1 - February 15 July 1 - August
  15 The market currently hosts more than 150 vendors\, and many categories
  are at capacity. At this time\, we are not accepting applications from mo
 st non-farm-based vendors until the next application period. However\, we 
 are always interested in hearing from local producers of fresh produce\, m
 eat\, dairy\, and other farm-based products. Before applying\, please revi
 ew our vendor categories and eligibility requirements in the Market Rules 
 & Regulations. Questions can be directed to market@moncuspark.org. If you'
 d like to learn more\, visit the market website: Market at Moncus Park Que
 stions? Reach the market team anytime at market@moncuspark.org. To learn m
 ore\, visit the market's website: marketatmoncuspark.com\n\nhttps://moncus
 park.org/calendar-events/farmersmarket/
URL:https://moncuspark.org/calendar-events/farmersmarket/
